---
title: Collection and Identification
sidebar:
  label: Collection and identification
  order: 3
---

The `Collection & Identification` card stores the core specimen metadata, in
this order on screen:

| Field | Notes |
| --- | --- |
| Field ID | The cataloger's field number or a formatted project number. Use `Edit field ID` to switch the type for this specimen; NAHPU asks you to confirm, removes the old identifier, and does not reuse numbers already taken. |
| `Museum ID` | Optional museum catalog or accession number. Shown after `Show more`, or once it has a value. |
| `Cataloger` | The person who catalogs the specimen. Choosing one also sets `Preparator` and `Determiner`. |
| `Preparator` | The person who prepared the specimen or voucher. |
| `Condition` | The specimen's condition, from the list in Settings. |
| `Collection date`, `Collection time` | When the specimen was collected. |
| `Prep. date`, `Prep. time` | When the specimen was prepared. |

The **Identification** part of the card holds:

| Field | Notes |
| --- | --- |
| `Taxon` | A record from the project's taxon registry. |
| `Determiner` | The person who identified the specimen. |
| `ID Confidence` | `Low`, `Medium`, or `High`. |
| `Identification Method` | Optional evidence used. Appears once `ID Confidence` is set. |

## Taxonomy

The `Taxon Info` card is read from the taxon selected in `Collection & Identification`.
It shows class, order, and family in the specimen form. Select `View details` to
review the full taxonomy record, including:

- the record's `Rank`;
- kingdom and phylum, taken from the registry when recorded and inferred from
  class otherwise;
- class, order, family, genus, and — when the record reaches those ranks —
  species and subspecies, plus authors and common name;
- Red List category, CITES status, country status, and notes when present;
- the number of records that use the taxon, and a QR code to share it.
